  6. TWO FALSE POSITIVES, PRE-EMPTED

  spring-retry is an application library in this reactor, a root version property consumed by
  three child modules, and has nothing to do with test reruns. No POM sets a rerun count and
  no retry plugin is declared anywhere in the 145 POMs, so a baseline failure is real and
  reproducible, and fail-fast is safe.
  The coverage plugin's eight package-glob excludes in the root aggregator exclude packages
  from coverage MEASUREMENT only. They disable no test, and none of them matches the person
  plugin package. Relatedly and bindingly: the coverage prepare-agent execution declares a
  destination file and no property name, so it communicates with the test runner through the
  default argument-line property export. A unit-test-runner declaration must therefore not set
  a literal argument-line element, or instrumentation is silently severed and the check goal
  evaluates an empty data set against its minimum line-coverage ratio, which is a false pass.
  Instrumentation must be verifiably live.

